# ocservia installer configuration template.
#
# Copy this file to ./install.env in the directory you run the installer
# from (any configuration directory for either versioned Stage-1 bootstrap;
# the release checkout root only when running a checkout installer directly);
# it is git-ignored there and never makes the clean-release-checkout check fail.
#
# Parsing contract (deploy/lib/install-env.sh):
# - Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored; every other line
#   must be KEY=VALUE. A single static outer layer of matching quotes is
#   removed; nothing is ever expanded or executed.
# - Variables exported in the invoking shell always win over this file —
#   including ones explicitly exported empty; keys absent from both fall
#   back to the installer defaults.
# - Any key outside the allowlist of the installer you are running fails
#   closed. KEEP ONLY THE SECTION FOR THE HOST YOU ARE INSTALLING: the
#   Controller installer rejects the managed-node keys and vice versa.
#
# This template holds no secrets: protected material (tokens, private
# keys, certificates, passwords) is provisioned through your protected
# channel and referenced by path only.

## Controller (deploy/production/install.sh) ################################
#
# Public hostname and HTTPS address the Controller is served on.
#OCSERV_PUBLIC_HOST=controller.example.com
#OCSERV_HTTPS_ADDRESS=127.0.0.1
#OCSERV_CONTROLLER_PUBLIC_URL=https://controller.example.com
#
# Authentication and external services.
#OCSERV_OIDC_ISSUER=https://id.example.com
#OCSERV_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=ocservia
#OCSERV_CERTIFICATE_SIGNER_URL=https://pki.example.com/v1
#OCSERV_OTEL_BACKEND_ENDPOINT=otel.example.com:4317
#OCSERV_AUDIT_EVENT_KEY_ID=audit-event-v1
#
# Controller public Iroh EndpointID (64 lowercase hex) and the two
# dedicated production relay URLs.
#OCSERV_CONTROLLER_ENDPOINT_ID=replace-with-64-lowercase-hex-controller-endpoint-id
#OCSERV_RELAY_URL_A=https://relay-a.example.com
#OCSERV_RELAY_URL_B=https://relay-b.example.com
#
# Protected directories outside the checkout.
#OCSERV_SECRET_DIR=/protected/ocservia-secrets
#OCSERV_BACKUP_DIR=/protected/ocservia-backups
#OCSERV_CONTROLLER_STATE_ROOT=/var/lib/ocservia-controller
#
# Release trust: the independently provisioned release-signing public key.
#OCSERV_CONTROLLER_RELEASE_PUBLIC_KEY=/etc/ocservia/controller-release-signing.pub.pem
#
# Backup tunables.
#OCSERV_BACKUP_INTERVAL_SECONDS=300
#OCSERV_BACKUP_RETENTION_COUNT=4

## Managed node (deploy/managed-node/install.sh) ############################
#
# Controller binding and the two dedicated relay URLs.
#CONTROLLER_ENDPOINT_ID=replace-with-64-lowercase-hex-controller-endpoint-id
#RELAY_URL_A=https://relay-a.example.com
#RELAY_URL_B=https://relay-b.example.com
#
# Paths to operator-provisioned protected material (never the material
# itself).
#RELAY_ACCESS_TOKEN_SOURCE=/protected/relay-access-token
#CONTROLLER_COMMAND_VERIFICATION_KEY_SOURCE=/protected/controller-command-verification-key.pem
#BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN_SOURCE=/protected/node-bootstrap-token
#
# Release trust anchor and its expected SHA-256 fingerprint (the same
# anchor the durable upgrader uses).
#TRUSTED_RELEASE_KEY=/etc/ocservia/release-signing.pub.pem
#EXPECTED_RELEASE_KEY_SHA256=replace-with-64-lowercase-hex-fingerprint
#
# Non-sensitive enrollment tunables.
#ENROLLMENT_ENVIRONMENT=production
#USER_PASSWORD_SEAL_KEY_ID=user-password-v1
#P12_PASSWORD_SEAL_KEY_ID=p12-password-v1
